<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= pageTitle %> - Blogger AI</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background-color: #1a202c;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 720px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 30px;
            background-color: #2d3748;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }
        h1 { color: #4299e1; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 2rem; }
        .subtitle { color: #a0aec0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 24px; }
        .message { margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; }
        .message.error { background-color: #742a2a; color: #feb2b2; border: 1px solid #9b2c2c; }
        .message.success { background-color: #22543d; color: #9ae6b4; border: 1px solid #276749; }
        .status-box {
            background-color: #1a202c;
            border: 1px solid #4a5568;
            border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 14px 16px;
            margin-bottom: 24px;
        }
        .status-box p { margin: 4px 0; }
        .status-box .label { color: #a0aec0; font-weight: bold; }
        .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 2px 10px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .badge.ok { background-color: #22543d; color: #9ae6b4; }
        .badge.bad { background-color: #742a2a; color: #feb2b2; }
        .badge.pending { background-color: #744210; color: #fbd38d; }
        .mono { font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; word-break: break-all; }
        .error-detail { color: #feb2b2; }
        form { margin-bottom: 20px; }
        label { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: bold; color: #a0aec0; }
        input[type="password"] {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            border: 1px solid #4a5568;
            border-radius: 4px;
            background-color: #1a202c;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        input[type="password"]::placeholder { color: #718096; }
        .hint { color: #a0aec0; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 8px; }
        .hint code { background-color: #1a202c; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 3px; color: #90cdf4; }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            background-color: #4299e1;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin-top: 12px;
        }
        button:hover { background-color: #2b6cb0; }
        button.secondary {
            background-color: #4a5568;
            margin-left: 8px;
        }
        button.secondary:hover { background-color: #374151; }
        .clear-form { display: inline; }
        .instructions {
            background-color: #1a202c;
            border: 1px solid #4a5568;
            border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 12px 16px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .instructions summary {
            cursor: pointer;
            color: #90cdf4;
            font-weight: bold;
            outline: none;
        }
        .instructions summary:hover { color: #4299e1; }
        .instructions ol { margin: 12px 0 4px 0; padding-left: 22px; }
        .instructions li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .instructions code {
            background-color: #2d3748;
            padding: 1px 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            color: #90cdf4;
            word-break: break-all;
        }
        .instructions a { color: #90cdf4; }
        .error-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        .error-table th, .error-table td { border: 1px solid #4a5568; padding: 6px 10px; text-align: left; }
        .error-table th { background-color: #2d3748; color: #a0aec0; }
        .error-table td:first-child { color: #feb2b2; white-space: nowrap; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Database Setup</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Connect your MongoDB Atlas account by pasting your connection string.</p>

        <% if (message) { %>
            <div class="message <%= error ? 'error' : 'success' %>"><%= message %></div>
        <% } %>

        <div class="status-box">
            <p>
                <span class="label">Connection status:</span>
                <% if (db.connected) { %>
                    <span class="badge ok">Connected</span>
                <% } else if (db.state === 2) { %>
                    <span class="badge pending">Connecting…</span>
                <% } else { %>
                    <span class="badge bad">Not connected</span>
                <% } %>
            </p>
            <p><span class="label">Connection string:</span>
                <% if (db.uriMasked) { %>
                    <span class="mono"><%= db.uriMasked %></span>
                    (<%= db.uriSource === 'env' ? 'from MONGODB_URI environment variable' : 'saved in-app' %>)
                <% } else { %>
                    <span class="error-detail">not set</span>
                <% } %>
            </p>
            <% if (db.lastError) { %>
                <p><span class="label">Last error:</span> <span class="error-detail mono"><%= db.lastError %></span></p>
            <% } %>
        </div>

        <details class="instructions">
            <summary>📘 New here? Step-by-step: how to get your MongoDB credentials (free, ~5 minutes)</summary>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Create a MongoDB Atlas account</strong> — go to
                    <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register</a>
                    and sign up for free (Google sign-in works).
                </li>
                <li><strong>Create a free cluster</strong> — click <em>Build a Database</em>, choose the free
                    <strong>M0</strong> plan (Shared), pick any cloud provider and region, name your cluster,
                    then click <em>Create</em>. It takes 1–3 minutes to finish.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Create a database user</strong> — in the left menu go to
                    <em>Database Access</em> → <em>Add New Database User</em>. Choose <em>Password</em>
                    authentication, enter a username and a strong password, then <em>Add User</em>.
                    <br>⚠️ Keep this username &amp; password — you need them for the connection string.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Allow access from anywhere</strong> — go to <em>Network Access</em> →
                    <em>Add IP Address</em> → select <em>Allow access from anywhere</em> (<code>0.0.0.0/0</code>)
                    → <em>Confirm</em>. Required because this app's servers use changing IP addresses.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Copy the connection string</strong> — go to <em>Database</em> → your cluster →
                    <em>Connect</em> → <em>Drivers</em> → select <em>Node.js</em>. Copy the string starting with
                    <code>mongodb+srv://</code>. It looks like:
                    <br><code>mongodb+srv://dbUser:&lt;password&gt;@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&amp;w=majority</code>
                </li>
                <li><strong>Replace &lt;password&gt;</strong> with your database user's real password.
                    If the password contains special characters, URL-encode them first
                    (<code>@</code> → <code>%40</code>, <code>:</code> → <code>%3A</code>, <code>/</code> → <code>%2F</code>,
                    <code>#</code> → <code>%23</code>, <code>?</code> → <code>%3F</code>).
                    Example: <code>p@ssw0rd</code> → <code>p%40ssw0rd</code>.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Paste it in the box below</strong> and click <em>Save &amp; Connect</em>.
                    The app connects automatically and keeps retrying until it succeeds.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </details>

        <form action="/setup/save" method="POST">
            <label for="mongodbUri">MongoDB connection string (from Atlas → Connect → Drivers)</label>
            <input type="password" id="mongodbUri" name="mongodbUri"
                   placeholder="mongodb+srv://dbUser:password@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/"
                   autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
            <button type="submit">Save &amp; Connect</button>
        </form>

        <% if (db.uriSource === 'in-app') { %>
            <form class="clear-form" action="/setup/clear" method="POST"
                  onsubmit="return confirm('Remove the saved connection string and stop using this database?');">
                <button type="submit" class="secondary">Remove Saved Connection</button>
            </form>
        <% } %>

        <p class="hint">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> the string is stored on this server (never in git) and the app keeps
            retrying automatically until it connects. For persistence across redeploys, also set
            <code>MONGODB_URI</code> in Render → Service → Environment — the in-app value takes precedence
            while it exists. Make sure your Atlas <strong>Network Access</strong> includes
            <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> (allow from anywhere).
        </p>
        <p class="hint"><a href="/healthz" style="color:#90cdf4;">Check /healthz</a></p>

        <details class="instructions">
            <summary>❓ Connection failing? Common errors and what they mean</summary>
            <table class="error-table">
                <tr><th>Error you see</th><th>What it means / how to fix it</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Authentication failed</td>
                    <td>Wrong database username or password in the connection string. Re-check step 3 and step 6 above.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>querySrv ENOTFOUND …</td>
                    <td>Cluster hostname is wrong or the cluster is still being created. Re-copy the string from Atlas → Connect (step 5).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>not authorized</td>
                    <td>Atlas Network Access doesn't allow this server's IP. Add <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> (allow from anywhere) in Atlas → Network Access (step 4).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>MONGODB_URI is not defined</td>
                    <td>No connection string is configured yet — paste one in the box above and click Save &amp; Connect.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Bad auth / bad password</td>
                    <td>The password contains unencoded special characters. URL-encode it (step 6).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Timed out</td>
                    <td>Temporary network issue — the app retries automatically every 60s, just wait a minute.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </details>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
